The SB16 DSP's Creative ADPCM decoder (4-bit, 2.6-bit, and 2-bit) ports the
step/adjust tables and predictor arithmetic of DOSBox-X's decode_ADPCM_*
functions (https://github.com/joncampbell123/dosbox-x, src/hardware/sblaster.cpp,
(C) 2002-2020 The DOSBox Team and the DOSBox-X contributors, GPLv2-or-later),
reimplemented in Rust for IzarraVM.
Distira's SST-1 DAC-backdoor handshake and W-buffer depth encoding follow the
behavior of 86Box's Voodoo emulation (https://86box.net, © 2008-2020 Sarah
Walker and contributors, GPLv2-or-later), reimplemented in Rust for IzarraVM.
Native MIDI synthesis links FluidSynth 2.5.6 and Munt/libmt32emu 2.8.2
statically under LGPL-2.1-or-later. FluidSynth's SF3 reader uses libsndfile
1.2.2 under LGPL-2.1-or-later. That build also contains an Apache-2.0 ALAC
codec, GSM 6.10 code under TU-Berlin-1.0, G72x code under the Sun source-code
terms, and OpusFile-based code under BSD-3-Clause. Munt's linked libmt32emu
contains Micael Hildenborg's SHA-1 implementation under BSD-3-Clause.
The linked libogg 1.3.6, libvorbis 1.3.7, FLAC 1.4.3, and Opus 1.5.2 libraries
use their BSD licenses. FluidSynth also uses GCEM under Apache-2.0. The full
source archives contain additional test, documentation, build, and training
files under their own terms. Exact sources, notices, hashes, and relinking
instructions are in crates/izarravm-native-synth/vendor. Roland ROMs are not
distributed.
