TOKAEMM.SYS (the XMS/UMB/EMS memory manager and V86 monitor) is a 386MAX
adaptation: its VCPI 1.0 server and its V86 privileged-instruction emulation
(the INT 67h AH=DEh handlers, the DE0C mode switch, and the MOV CRn/DRn /
CLTS / LMSW emulation-vs-reflect surface) follow the mechanisms of 386MAX and
its DPMIONE outgrowth (https://github.com/sudleyplace/386MAX, © 1987-98
Qualitas, Inc. and © 1990-2012 Sudley Place Software / Bob Smith, GPLv3),
adapted to the Izarra3000's virtual hardware and reimplemented in NASM for
IzarraVM. The VCPI 1.0 interface follows the Virtual Control Program
Interface specification (© 1987-89 Phar Lap Software, Inc. and Quarterdeck
Office Systems).

